1wa5|v|To cause to become sour; to cause to turn from sweet to sour; as, exposure to the air sours many substances. ; To make cold and unproductive, as soil. ; To make unhappy, uneasy, or less agreeable. ; To cause or permit to become harsh or unkindly. ; To macerate, and render fit for plaster or mortar; as, to sour lime for business purposes. ; To become sour; to turn from sweet to sour; as, milk soon sours in hot weather; a kind temper sometimes sours in adversity.	o:1a9f,50,1;slp,39,1~1a9f,50,1;slp,39,1	d:165x,11,2~165x,11,2
