1wc3|v|To sew. See Sew. ; To scatter, as seed, upon the earth; to plant by strewing; as, to sow wheat. Also used figuratively: To spread abroad; to propagate. ; To scatter seed upon, in, or over; to supply or stock, as land, with seeds. Also used figuratively: To scatter over; to besprinkle. ; To scatter seed for growth and the production of a crop; -- literally or figuratively.	o:ery,88,3~ery,88,3
